The extra room is stepped (0.5, 0.75, 1.0 of the missing time, one seed each) because both simple sizings failed on the sample video. Scaling the request by slot/speech assumed F5's edge silence is proportional; it is not, and adding the whole missing time also overshot (segments 1 and 4 came out 15-16% long) because F5 pads a longer request with less silence. Worse, generous room made F5 speak the romanized reference transcript before the line ('Kaite mitai to omoimasu. What do you think...'), which the check rejected on every seed; half the missing time already reached ~100% coverage cleanly. Correction runs only after a take passes the check, reuses that take's seed first, and accepts a longer take only if it passes the check again and fits within FIT_MAX_SPEED, so it can never trade a correct line for a longer wrong one. The per-speaker silence estimate proposed in the issue was skipped: the stepped second pass reached the 90% target on every line, at about twice the TTS takes. extra_words was added after a leaked 'Sakana,' slipped through at WER 0.14: the check only looked for missing expected words, never for inserted ones.
